---
description: Prefer named exports; ban default exports except Next.js route entries
alwaysApply: true
---

# Named exports only

Export with named exports (`export function`, `export const`, `export type`). Do not use `export default`.

Importers must use the real export name:

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
export default function PromptEditForm() {}
import Form from "./prompts"

// ✅ GOOD
export function PromptEditForm() {}
import { PromptEditForm } from "./prompts"
```

Exception: Next.js App Router files that require default export — `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `not-found.tsx`, `template.tsx`, `default.tsx`. Co-located helpers and components in those files still use named exports.
